<title>UK: Tomkins to sell small subsidiaries - paper.</title>
<headline>Tomkins to sell small subsidiaries - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diversified manufacturer Tomkins Plc is planning to shed its smaller subsidiaries to free up the time of leading company executives, the Sunday Times said.</p>
<p>The disposals are likely to be concentrated on the company's &quot;services to industry&quot; division, although smaller businesses in other divisions may also be sold, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Tomkins, best known for its ownership of Ranks Hovis McDougall's food business and the Smith &amp; Wesson handguns company, has 74 subsidiaries, the Sunday Times said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom + 44 171 542 7792</p>
